    "narrative": "With the 2026 season winding down, today\u2019s focus for Ghost Ride the WHIP centers on exploiting mid-tier opposing arms to secure crucial counting stats. **Brice Turang** headlines our active roster today, boasting a strong 64.99 efficiency score. His matchup against Michael King (4.39 xERA) is a primary target; King\u2019s vulnerability to aggressive baserunning aligns perfectly with our need to bolster stolen bases, as **Brice Turang** holds a significant efficiency edge despite the 4% penalty for King\u2019s ability to control the run game. We are counting on **Brice Turang** in the two-hole to set the table, as his current recency trend and the +8% boost from the batting order make him a high-floor asset for today\u2019s 5x5 Roto push.\n\nThe decision to keep **Dalton Rushing** on the bench was the most difficult call of the morning, as his 38.77 score fell just shy of our threshold. While **Dalton Rushing** benefits from a generally favorable matchup against Ray Kerr, the combination of his likely ninth-order placement and the disadvantageous L/L platoon split acted as an anchor, dragging his projection below our mandatory 40-point efficiency floor. With **Corbin Carroll**, **Jose Caballero**, and **Josh Naylor** all sitting due to scheduled team off-days, our bench depth is intentionally thin, forcing us to lean heavily on the remaining active bats like **James Wood**, **Mickey Moniak**, and **Seiya Suzuki** to carry the offensive load. Investors should keep a close eye on the late-breaking lineups for any changes to the projected batting orders of **Giancarlo Stanton**, **Vinnie Pasquantino**, and **Tyler Soderstrom**, as shifting lineup protections remain the highest-variance variable in today\u2019s scoring model. Be advised: if any weather fronts impact the evening games, we may pivot to defensive utility players like **Max Muncy** or **Gabriel Moreno** to preserve our remaining games-played caps.",
